invariant: INV-21
file: handshake.c
catches: test/e2e.sh
builds: bin/tlsclient bin/tlsclient_ecdsa bin/tlsclient_ca bin/tlsclient_ca_ecdsa bin/example_psk bin/example_pinned bin/example_ca
reason: committing the epoch on the chain verdict alone lets a certificate
  that never proves possession of its key raise the device's stored
  epoch, which outlives the session. epoch_commit asserts on
  server_finished_ok, so the moved call faults on the first CA leg —
  before it can write, and whether or not epoch callbacks are
  configured

--- old
    rc = epoch_check(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
    rc = epoch_check(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
    // Symmetry with the rejects: judge and record in one place.
    epoch_commit(h);
